// Reaching C from Cufet, part two: memory that C owns, and axioms that travel.
//
// `foreign.cufe` next door covers axioms and the values you hand them. This one covers what is
// left of the boundary — a POINTER C allocated, reading through it, giving it back, and passing
// an axiom around as a value instead of calling it where it is written.
//
// The C here is libc and nothing else, so this program prints the same thing on every machine.
// Note what is NOT printed anywhere below: an address. Two runs of the same program get different
// pointers, so a printed one could never be compared — an address shows itself as `<address>`.

Pull a rabbit.
    Pull a book on the c-language.
        // ── An address, and who gives it back ────────────────────────────────
        //
        // `voidable address` is the only shape a pointer crosses in. Voidable because NULL is how
        // C says it had nothing to give, and every allocator says it that way — so the failure
        // lands in the mechanism Cufet already has rather than in a new one.
        //
        // `and free it with hand-back` names the axiom that frees what this one produces. It runs
        // on every way out of the block, an exception included, and it runs once per acquisition
        // — not once per name you bind the result to.
        Define c-language number hand-back, given (the address held), as [(free(the held), 0)].
        Define c-language voidable address copy-of, given (the text subject),
            as [strdup(the subject)], and free it with hand-back.

        Define the phrase as "hello, world".
        Define held as cast copy-of on (the phrase).

        // ── Reading through it ───────────────────────────────────────────────
        //
        // `the text at <address>` is the ONLY read there is, and it always COPIES: the bytes
        // belong to C, which may free or overwrite them whenever it likes. Reading a struct or a
        // scalar is not offered and is not missing — an axiom can do that in C, where the layout
        // is known, and hand back something Cufet understands.
        //
        // Reading through a void address is void, not a crash.
        Define echoed as (the text at held) but void is "(nothing)".
        State "C kept a copy of: {echoed}.".
        State "It is the same text Cufet started with: {echoed is the phrase}.".
        // An address prints as `<address>`, never as its value — two runs get different pointers,
        // so a printed one could never be compared between them.
        State held.

        // ── An axiom is a value ──────────────────────────────────────────────
        //
        // An axiom that says what it gives back can be passed around unrun and run wherever it
        // lands. The type is written the way its declaration reads, with `given (…)` saying what
        // running it takes — the same spelling a function type uses.
        //
        // The foreign text is still fixed where it was written. Nothing is assembled from strings
        // and nothing can be injected; what moves is the axiom itself.
        Define c-language number length-of, given (the text subject), as [(int)strlen(the subject)].
        Define c-language number first-code, given (the text subject), as [(int)(the subject)[0]].

        Define the measures as a series of c-language number axiom given (the text)
            with (length-of, first-code).

        State "Two axioms, chosen by the loop rather than by the text:".
        For each measure in the measures, repeat:
            State "  C answers {cast measure on ("abc")}.".
        Done.

        // Which one runs is decided at run time, so a function can take an axiom the way it takes
        // anything else. There is no `cast length-of` anywhere in this body — it runs whatever it
        // was handed.
        Bind number to twice-over, given (the c-language number axiom given (the text) job,
                                          the text subject):
            Return (cast job on (subject)) * 2.
        Done.

        State "Twice the length of \"abc\" is {cast twice-over on (length-of, "abc")}.".
    Done.
Done.
